<!-- 2 Problem -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Context &amp; problem &middot; Taiwan hospitals first</div>
  <h1>Hospitals must share records &mdash; and the law now punishes leaks</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every workplace hands out documents about people &mdash; hospitals, courts, insurers, agencies. We start where the
    need is sharpest. Every one of Taiwan's <b>3.35 million discharges a year</b> leaves a chart that may later be requested for
    research, insurance claims, disputes or copies. Each released copy must first be stripped of personal data &mdash; today, by hand.</p>
  <div class="grid4" style="margin-bottom:20px">
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">IRB &amp; research</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Data release</h3><p>Research use is lawful only if the data &ldquo;cannot identify the person&rdquo; &mdash; also after combining it with other data (PDPA Art.&nbsp;6, MOJ).</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Records office</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Copies on request</h3><p>Hospitals must provide copies of medical records (Medical Care Act Art.&nbsp;71); third parties see only what they may.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Legal &amp; QA</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Disputes &amp; claims</h3><p>Scanned charts, consent forms, prescriptions with seals and signatures go to courts and insurers.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Health data</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Secondary use</h3><p>The NHI Data Management Act (in force Aug 2026) adds an opt-out and NT$2&ndash;10M fines for misuse.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid3">
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>People miss identifiers</h3><p>Single clinicians found only <b>81&nbsp;%</b> of identifiers on average (63&ndash;94&nbsp;%); three reviewers still missed some. Manual de-identification took ~87&nbsp;s per note.</p></div>
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>Cloud AI is off-limits</h3><p>Medical records are special-category data &mdash; hospitals will not send them to an external API. The tool must run inside the hospital.</p></div>
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>Stakes are rising</h3><p>PDPA amendment (Nov 2025): breach notification and a dedicated regulator; security failures already cost up to <b>NT$15M</b> per uncorrected instance.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Sources: MOHW hospital statistics 2025; PDPA Art. 6, 12, 48 and Enforcement Rules Art. 17; Medical Care Act Art. 71; NHI Data Management Act (MOHW 2025-12, in force 2026-08-10);
    Neamatullah et al., BMC Med Inform Decis Mak 2008; Dorr et al., Methods Inf Med 2006. Details: docs/MARKET_RESEARCH.md.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span>2</span></div>
</section>

